.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt SHA256SUM 1
.Os NovaOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm sha256sum
.Nd compute and verify SHA-256 file digests
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b | Fl t
.Op Fl z
.Op Fl -tag
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl c
.Op Fl -ignore-missing
.Op Fl -quiet | Fl -status | Fl w
.Op Fl -strict
.Op Ar manifest ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read standard input when no file is supplied or its name is a dash.
Relative manifest paths start at the working directory.
.Bl -tag -width "--ignore-missing"
.It Fl b , Fl -binary
Use the binary marker *.
.It Fl t , Fl -text
Use a space for the text marker.
Both input modes preserve all bytes.
.It Fl z , Fl -zero
Emit NUL after each record and use raw filenames.
.It Fl -tag
Write a BSD-style checksum record.
.It Fl c , Fl -check
Check the files listed in each manifest.
.It Fl -ignore-missing
Skip missing files and require at least one match in each manifest.
.It Fl -quiet
Omit matching records.
.It Fl -status
Suppress per-file results and summaries.
.It Fl -strict
Treat malformed lines as failures.
.It Fl w , Fl -warn
Report each malformed line.
.It Fl -help , Fl -version
Print help or the component version.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.
Differences and errors yield a nonzero exit status.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
sha256sum file.bin
SHA256SUM_READ_1=file.bin
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
cat file.bin | sha256sum
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
In nsh each SHA256SUM_READ_N selects one permitted manifest input.
Use the same spelling as the trusted release inventory.
